# ims-pre-move-update-must-confirm-before-physical-move

Rule 10: the inventory management system (IMS) location update must be submitted AND confirmed before any physical lot movement begins; if IMS is degraded/slow, wait for confirmation regardless of schedule pressure.

## Procedures
- 1. Before touching or moving any lot, submit the pre-move location update to IMS with the new destination.
- 2. Wait for IMS to confirm the transaction. Per degraded-performance advisory (30–90 second commit time), do not begin physical movement during this window.
- 3. If the transaction times out, retry; do not move the lot until a confirmation is received.
- 4. If IMS goes fully offline (outage), hold all physical movement until the system recovers — operators waiting is an acceptable consequence.
- 5. Only after IMS confirms the location update may you physically pick up and move the lot.

## Conventions
- IMS update always precedes physical movement — the system of record must lead the physical state.
- Schedule pressure from operators or managers does not justify moving before IMS confirms.

